00:42:37.100 --> 00:42:51.970
<v Kimu Elolia>I'm seeing police on horseback chasing protesters, going around with wooden sticks and just beating people as they rode through, and then protesters retaliating and running back and chasing the police. And then they kind of regain their ground.
<v Kimu Elolia>我看到骑马的警察追赶抗议者，拿着木棍四处走动，骑马冲过时就开始殴打人们，然后抗议者反击并跑回去追赶警察。然后他们重新占领了阵地。

00:42:51.970 --> 00:42:54.600
<v Ira Glass>Oh, so the line is moving forward and backward.
<v Ira Glass>哦，所以战线在向前和向后移动。

00:42:54.600 --> 00:43:05.320
<v Kimu Elolia>Yeah, it's going back and forth. And police are shooting tear gas canisters. One of them hits a guy in the leg, and he picks it up and drop kicks it like a soccer ball back towards the police.
<v Kimu Elolia>是的，它在来回移动。警察在发射催泪瓦斯罐。其中一个击中了一个人的腿，他把它捡起来，像踢足球一样把它踢回警察那边。

00:43:05.320 --> 00:43:08.980
<v Ira Glass>And these protests began a couple of months ago over a proposed tax hike, right?
<v Ira Glass>这些抗议活动是几个月前因为提议提高税收而开始的，对吧？

00:43:08.980 --> 00:43:17.920
<v Kimu Elolia>Yeah, there were these really punitive tax hikes impacting a lot of Kenyan everyday items, like cooking oil, flour, tampons, even diapers.
<v Kimu Elolia>是的，有一些非常惩罚性的增税影响了许多肯尼亚的日常用品，比如食用油、面粉、卫生棉条，甚至尿布。

00:43:17.920 --> 00:43:22.060
<v Ira Glass>And this is the sort of thing, like, the government needed the money because there's IMF loans and stuff to pay off?
<v Ira Glass>政府需要这些钱，因为有国际货币基金组织的贷款和之类的东西要偿还？

00:43:22.060 --> 00:43:26.140
<v Kimu Elolia>Yeah, it was supposed to be the solution to pay back the IMF.
<v Kimu Elolia>是的，它本应是偿还国际货币基金组织的解决方案。

00:43:26.140 --> 00:43:28.420
<v Ira Glass>But then it became something more than that.
<v Ira Glass>但后来它变得不仅仅是那样了。

00:43:28.420 --> 00:43:42.940
<v Kimu Elolia>Yeah, it became this huge movement where people, especially young people, were just rejecting just the status quo of the way the Kenyan government's been operating. Politicians flaunting their Rolex watches, their Bentleys.
<v Kimu Elolia>是的，它变成了一场巨大的运动，人们，特别是年轻人，只是拒绝了肯尼亚政府运作方式的现状。政客们炫耀他们的劳力士手表，他们的宾利汽车。

00:43:42.940 --> 00:43:43.930
<v Ira Glass>This is on social media.
<v Ira Glass>这是在社交媒体上。

00:43:43.930 --> 00:43:54.730
<v Kimu Elolia>On social media, while they're being asked to pay for way more for these regular everyday items. And young people make up-- 75% of the population is under 35.
<v Kimu Elolia>在社交媒体上，而他们被要求为这些常规日常用品支付更多的费用。年轻人占人口的比例——75%的人口在35岁以下。

00:43:54.730 --> 00:43:55.720
<v Ira Glass>Oh, wow.
<v Ira Glass>哦，哇。

00:43:55.720 --> 00:44:14.050
<v Kimu Elolia>Yeah, and the median age in the country is around 20 years old. And this young generation, they're crossing tribal lines. In the past, tribes, they typically act like de facto political parties. And so one tribe will gain control of the country, and another tribe will be protesting.
<v Kimu Elolia>是的，这个国家的年龄中位数在20岁左右。年轻一代，他们正在跨越部落界限。在过去，部落通常充当事实上的政党。所以一个部落将获得国家的控制权，另一个部落将会抗议。

00:44:14.050 --> 00:44:18.480
<v Ira Glass>Oh, so now people from different tribes are protesting together in this way that's new.
<v Ira Glass>哦，所以现在来自不同部落的人正在以这种新的方式一起抗议。

00:44:18.480 --> 00:44:23.500
<v Kimu Elolia>Yeah, these young people are united. And they really just see themselves as Kenyans.
<v Kimu Elolia>是的，这些年轻人是团结的。他们真的只是把自己视为肯尼亚人。

00:44:23.500 --> 00:44:33.430
<v Ira Glass>So I know that you got interested in the front line protesters who go to the part of the line where it's the most dangerous. And you started talking to one of them and his mom. Who is he?
<v Ira Glass>所以我知道你对前线抗议者感兴趣，他们去最危险的一线。你开始和他们中的一个以及他的妈妈交谈。他是谁？

00:44:33.430 --> 00:44:52.870
<v Kimu Elolia>So he goes by Ospina. Ospina is 27. He's a law student. My sister introduced me to him, and she was telling me about this guy who-- he's in Kibera, which is a neighborhood in Nairobi. It's one of the largest slums in all of Africa. You really can't go anywhere in the neighborhood without seeing the places he's touched and the projects he's done.
<v Kimu Elolia>他叫奥斯皮纳。奥斯皮纳27岁。他是法学院学生。我姐姐把我介绍给他，她跟我说这个家伙——他在基贝拉，那是内罗毕的一个社区。它是整个非洲最大的贫民窟之一。在那个社区里，你真的走到哪里都能看到他留下的足迹和他做过的项目。

00:44:52.870 --> 00:44:56.350
<v Ira Glass>And in these protests, he's going to the front lines, where most of the violence and arrests are happening.
<v Ira Glass>在这些抗议活动中，他去最前线，那里发生着最严重的暴力和逮捕。

00:44:56.350 --> 00:45:01.930
<v Kimu Elolia>Yeah, and because it's so dangerous, before he goes out each time, he says a prayer to himself.
<v Kimu Elolia>是的，因为太危险了，每次出去之前，他都会向自己祈祷。

00:45:01.930 --> 00:45:15.530
<v Ospina>So, God, as I'm leaving this place, protect me, guide me, and be with me. Bless our country. Be with my family. Bless my mother. I know she's praying with me. Amen.
<v Ospina>所以，上帝，当我离开这个地方时，保护我，指引我，与我同在。祝福我们的国家。与我的家人同在。祝福我的母亲。我知道她和我一起祈祷。阿门。

00:45:15.530 --> 00:45:20.660
<v Ira Glass>He's saying at the end there, bless my mother. What does his mom think of this, the fact that he goes to the front lines?
<v Ira Glass>他在结尾说祝福我的母亲。他妈妈怎么看这件事，他去前线的事？

00:45:20.660 --> 00:45:25.610
<v Kimu Elolia>His mom does not approve. She does not want him going at all.
<v Kimu Elolia>他妈妈不支持。她根本不想让他去。

00:45:25.610 --> 00:45:36.700
<v Ira Glass>And you put together this story about what this has done to the relationship and how they're managing with each other. Let's hear that now. In your story, the name that she asked us to call her is Anna.
<v Ira Glass>你整理了这个关于这对他关系造成的影响以及他们如何相处的故事。让我们现在听听那个。在你的故事里，她要求我们称呼她的名字是安娜。

00:45:36.700 --> 00:46:00.220
<v Kimu Elolia>In the beginning, when he started going to the protests, Ospina dealt with his mom by lying to her. He'd come back home from the front lines, shower the tear gas off, and drop by her house, pretending he'd been having a normal day. But he wasn't so good at keeping it a secret. Like, one day, at a protest, a TV crew put a mic in front of him and started interviewing him. Anna found out.
<v Kimu Elolia>起初，当他开始去抗议时，奥斯皮纳通过撒谎来应付妈妈。他会从前线回家，洗掉催泪瓦斯，顺便去她家，假装自己过着正常的一天。但他不太擅长保密。有一天，在抗议现场，一个电视摄制组把麦克风放在他面前开始采访他。安娜发现了。

00:46:00.220 --> 00:46:01.380
<v Anna>[SPEAKING SWAHILI]
<v Anna>（斯瓦希里语发言）

00:46:01.380 --> 00:46:09.260
<v Interpreter>My friend called me and told me that they have seen Ospina on TV. So I was calling Ospina.
<v Interpreter>我朋友打电话给我，告诉我他们已经在电视上看到奥斯皮纳了。所以我打电话给奥斯皮纳。

00:46:09.260 --> 00:46:18.140
<v Ospina>I was just at the middle of finishing my interview. Then the phone was ringing. Then I just see, ah, it's Mom. This woman is going to make it difficult for me.
<v Ospina>我当时正要完成我的采访。然后电话响了。然后我看到，啊，是妈妈。这个女人要让我的日子难过了。

00:46:18.140 --> 00:46:28.340
<v Interpreter>And I was like, where are you? And he was just not telling me. Then I was like, you were on TV for the protest. And he just kept laughing.
<v Interpreter>我问，你在哪里？他就是不告诉我。然后我说，你在电视上抗议。他只是不停地笑。

00:46:28.340 --> 00:46:29.750
<v Anna>[SPEAKING SWAHILI]
<v Anna>（斯瓦希里语发言）

00:46:29.750 --> 00:46:47.810
<v Ospina>My mom is funny when she's angry. She just starts yelling. [CHUCKLES] I'm like, I'm just home. Then she's like, you're lying. I've seen you on TV. Then I'm like, are you sure? Which station did you see me? I'm just home. Then she's like, I need you to come back right now.
<v Ospina>我妈妈生气的时候很有趣。她只是开始大喊大叫。（轻笑）我当时说，我正在家里。然后她说，你在撒谎。我在电视上看见你了。然后我说，你确定吗？你在哪个台看见我的？我正在家里。然后她说，我需要你马上回来。

00:46:47.810 --> 00:46:52.510
<v Interpreter>He was laughing, telling his friends, like, oh, my mom is panicked.
<v Interpreter>他在笑，告诉他的朋友们，就像，哦，我妈妈惊慌失措了。

00:46:52.510 --> 00:46:54.450
<v Interpreter>[CHUCKLING]
<v Interpreter>（轻笑）

00:46:54.450 --> 00:47:21.840
<v Kimu Elolia>Ospina and Anna have always been close. They talk all the time and tease each other. He lives a 10-minute walk away. Sometimes he'll bring his friends to the food stand she runs. It's called Mama Chapati. She's there all day in a blue or white dress. Ospina looks just like her. And over the years, he's done other stuff she didn't approve of at first and later came around to, like soccer, or football, whatever you want to call it.
<v Kimu Elolia>奥斯皮纳和安娜一直很亲近。他们总是聊天，互相调侃。他住在步行10分钟远的地方。有时他会带朋友去她经营的食品摊。它叫“妈妈查帕蒂”（Mama Chapati）。她整天穿着蓝色或白色的裙子待在那里。奥斯皮纳长得就像她。多年来，他做过其他她起初不赞同后来又接受的事情，比如足球，或者无论你管它叫什么。

00:47:21.840 --> 00:47:23.440
<v Anna>[SPEAKING SWAHILI]
<v Anna>（斯瓦希里语发言）

00:47:23.440 --> 00:47:37.490
<v Interpreter>He was keen on football. He used to play a lot. And I didn't see any value in playing football. In fact, it was such a nuisance because he'd come back home so dirty.
<v Interpreter>他很热衷足球。他过去常玩很多。我没看出踢球有什么价值。事实上，那真是一个麻烦，因为他回家时总是那么脏。

00:47:37.490 --> 00:47:58.460
<v Kimu Elolia>Then, when Ospina was 14, Anna and her husband couldn't afford to send him to school for a year. Anna says he took it well. She said he understood and was very grown-up about it. And then he took on odd jobs and played a lot of soccer. And she saw how happy it made him. He played so well that two soccer scouts got him a scholarship that put him back in the classroom.
<v Kimu Elolia>然后，当奥斯皮纳14岁时，安娜和丈夫负担不起让他上学一年。安娜说他接受得很好。她说他理解，并且表现得非常成熟。后来他做些零工，踢了很多足球。她看到了这让他有多开心。他踢得太好了，两个足球球探给了他奖学金，让他回到了课堂。

00:47:58.460 --> 00:48:26.790
<v Kimu Elolia>Anna was grateful. She grew up in a village and only got through the fifth grade and wanted more for her kids. A similar thing happened when Ospina decided to clean up their neighborhood. Kibera at the time had no roads, no streetlights, no trash collection. At first, when he told Anna he was going to pick up the trash himself, she thought he was joking. But within a few years, he was coordinating trash pickups for hundreds of houses. And she came around.
<v Kimu Elolia>安娜很感激。她在村子里长大，只读到了五年级，希望她的孩子们有更好的未来。当奥斯皮纳决定清理他们的社区时，类似的事情也发生了。当时的基贝拉没有道路，没有路灯，没有垃圾收集。起初，当他告诉安娜他要自己捡垃圾时，她以为他在开玩笑。但在几年内，他就在为数百户人家协调垃圾回收了。她最终接受了。

00:48:26.790 --> 00:48:39.490
<v Kimu Elolia>Ospina has so many projects going in Kibera these days-- organizing events and mentorship for kids, a greenhouse that grows and sells food, a water sanitation program-- lots of neighbors are pinning their hopes on him.
<v Kimu Elolia>奥斯皮纳这些天在基贝拉开展了许多项目——为孩子们组织活动和指导，一个种植和销售食物的温室，一个水卫生项目——许多邻居把希望寄托在他身上。

00:48:39.490 --> 00:48:41.610
<v Anna>[SPEAKING SWAHILI]
<v Anna>（斯瓦希里语发言）

00:48:41.610 --> 00:49:11.440
<v Interpreter>A lot of parents support him because he's helping their kids. What I tried to tell him-- and he never listens, and I never get across to him-- is how important he is to me. He is very, very important to me. And he has such a wonderful dream for our future, for the future of Kenya. So he told me about these dreams. He gave me these hopes.
<v Interpreter>很多家长支持他，因为他在帮助他们的孩子。我试着告诉他——但他从不听，我也从不让他明白——他对我有多重要。他对我非常非常重要。他为我们的未来，为肯尼亚的未来有着如此美好的梦想。所以他告诉我这些梦想。他给了我这些希望。

00:49:11.440 --> 00:49:29.300
<v Kimu Elolia>Up until now, Anna has liked Ospina's optimism. She liked the way he's pushed her. But she's lived through years of de facto one-party rule, seen protests get ruthlessly put down and activists get killed. And this time around, she doesn't understand where Ospina is coming from.
<v Kimu Elolia>直到现在，安娜都很喜欢奥斯皮纳的乐观。她喜欢他推动她的方式。但她经历过多年的事实上一党统治，目睹过抗议活动被无情镇压，活动人士被杀害。而这一次，她不理解奥斯皮纳从何而来。

00:49:29.300 --> 00:49:30.460
<v Anna>[SPEAKING SWAHILI]
<v Anna>（斯瓦希里语发言）

00:49:30.460 --> 00:49:44.320
<v Interpreter>Most of the time, he listens. But recently, he's just been deciding that I'm just someone who's afraid all the time, and I'm speaking out of fear. So he doesn't listen.
<v Interpreter>大多数时候，他听从。但最近，他只是认定我是一个总是害怕的人，我在出于恐惧说话。所以他不听。

00:49:44.320 --> 00:49:48.670
<v Kimu Elolia>Why do you feel like he thinks you're just speaking out of fear?
<v Kimu Elolia>为什么你觉得他认为你只是出于恐惧说话？

00:49:48.670 --> 00:49:52.090
<v Anna>[SPEAKING SWAHILI]
<v Anna>（斯瓦希里语发言）

00:49:52.090 --> 00:50:05.220
<v Interpreter>I think it's just an assumption, because I'm a woman, and I'm a mother. And men just assume that we are, we are always talking from fear.
<v Interpreter>我觉得这只是一个假设，因为我是个女人，是个母亲。男人们只是认为我们总是出于恐惧而说话。

00:50:05.220 --> 00:50:09.840
<v Kimu Elolia>Do you think that, in this case, it is out of fear?
<v Kimu Elolia>你认为在这种情况下，这是出于恐惧吗？

00:50:09.840 --> 00:50:12.190
<v Anna>[SPEAKING SWAHILI]
<v Anna>（斯瓦希里语发言）

00:50:12.190 --> 00:50:13.880
<v Anna>[LAUGHTER]
<v Anna>（笑声）

00:50:13.880 --> 00:50:25.970
<v Interpreter>Yes, he's right. Yeah, he's right. It's right. It was fear.
<v Interpreter>是的，他是对的。是的，他是对的。是对的。那是恐惧。

00:50:25.970 --> 00:50:37.310
<v Kimu Elolia>For the first few weeks of the protest, Anna and Ospina went back and forth, her telling him not to go, him lying to her, until things reached a boiling point on June 25.
<v Kimu Elolia>在抗议活动的最初几周，安娜和奥斯皮纳来来回回，她告诉他不要去，他跟她撒谎，直到6月25日达到了沸点。

00:50:37.310 --> 00:50:45.440
<v Man>Members of parliament have today passed the controversial finance bill with key amendments. The bill will now be forwarded to President William Ruto for assent.
<v Man>议会议员们今天通过了有争议的财政法案，并进行了关键修订。该法案现在将转交给威廉·鲁托总统签署。

00:50:45.440 --> 00:51:07.350
<v Kimu Elolia>Instead of killing the tax hikes like the protesters demanded, Kenya's parliament just made a few changes and pushed the bill through. And in response, Ospina and thousands of other protesters rushed to parliament, stormed the building, and some set part of it on fire on live TV. I remember it felt like the whole country was watching. It got violent.
<v Kimu Elolia>肯尼亚议会并没有像抗议者要求的那样取消增税，而是做了一些修改并强行通过了法案。作为回应，奥斯皮纳和成千上万的其他抗议者冲向议会，冲进大楼，一些人在直播中点燃了它。我记得感觉整个国家都在观看。它变得暴力了。

00:51:07.350 --> 00:51:11.800
<v Kimu Elolia>[GUNFIRE]
<v Kimu Elolia>（枪声）

00:51:11.800 --> 00:51:15.560
<v Anna>[SPEAKING SWAHILI]
<v Anna>（斯瓦希里语发言）

00:51:15.560 --> 00:51:39.260
<v Interpreter>A young kid from the neighborhood, came, and he was buying food from me. But he was out of breath, and he told me, Mom, they killed someone in front of me. And I saw his brains, and I had to crawl out. And I'm so, so lucky to have made it out. And you could see in his eyes that he has seen things that he shouldn't see, shouldn't have seen.
<v Interpreter>社区里的一个年轻人来了，他在买我的食物。但他上气不接下气，他告诉我，妈妈，他们在我面前杀了一个人。我看见了他的脑浆，我不得不爬出来。我太幸运了能逃出来。你可以从他的眼睛里看出他看到了不该看的东西。

00:51:39.260 --> 00:51:41.750
<v Kimu Elolia>That must have made you really scared.
<v Kimu Elolia>那一定让你非常害怕。

00:51:41.750 --> 00:51:43.690
<v Anna>[SPEAKING SWAHILI]
<v Anna>（斯瓦希里语发言）

00:51:43.690 --> 00:51:57.590
<v Interpreter>I was so scared because Ospina had said that they were going to go to parliament. And I tried calling his phone. I tried calling his phone. And his phone-- I couldn't reach him. I kept getting this voice message.
<v Interpreter>我太害怕了，因为奥斯皮纳说他们要去议会。我试着打他的电话。我一直打他的电话。而他的电话——我联系不上他。我一直收到这个语音留言。

00:51:57.590 --> 00:52:01.580
<v Anna>[SPEAKING SWAHILI]
<v Anna>（斯瓦希里语发言）

00:52:01.580 --> 00:52:23.920
<v Interpreter>I was restless. My stomach hurt. I had no energy. And I felt like something very bad is about to happen to someone that I depend on, someone who has my hopes, was the carrier of my hopes.
<v Interpreter>我坐立不安。我的胃很痛。我没有力气。我觉得我依赖的人，寄托我希望的人，承载我希望的人，就要发生非常糟糕的事情了。

00:52:23.920 --> 00:52:41.830
<v Kimu Elolia>Over a dozen people were killed. Anna called Ospina over and over, started asking people who passed her chapati stand if they'd seen him, called his siblings, called his friends, praying he'd pick up the phone. Then her daughter told her about something she saw on TV.
<v Kimu Elolia>十几个人被杀。安娜一遍又一遍地给奥斯皮纳打电话，开始询问路过她查帕蒂摊位的人是否见过他，给他的兄弟姐妹打电话，给他的朋友打电话，祈祷他能接电话。然后她的女儿告诉了她关于她在电视上看到的事情。

00:52:41.830 --> 00:52:44.170
<v Anna>[SPEAKING SWAHILI]
<v Anna>（斯瓦希里语发言）

00:52:44.170 --> 00:53:03.640
<v Interpreter>Lillian, my daughter, came and told me that she'd seen someone who was dressed exactly like Ospina who had been shot. And he was wearing the exact same shoes that Ospina was wearing. So I was so anxious. I couldn't-- I hadn't-- like, everything left me. All my life left me.
<v Interpreter>莉莲，我的女儿，过来说她看到一个穿得和奥斯皮纳一模一样的人被枪击了。而且他穿着奥斯皮纳穿的一模一样的鞋子。所以我太焦虑了。我无法——我没有——一切都离我而去。我所有的生命都离我而去。

00:53:03.640 --> 00:53:06.460
<v Anna>[SPEAKING SWAHILI]
<v Anna>（斯瓦希里语发言）

00:53:06.460 --> 00:53:14.640
<v Interpreter>Because my hopes and dreams and future lies with those children.
<v Interpreter>因为我的希望、梦想和未来都在那些孩子身上。

00:53:14.640 --> 00:53:18.010
<v Anna>[SPEAKING SWAHILI]
<v Anna>（斯瓦希里语发言）

00:53:18.010 --> 00:53:37.000
<v Interpreter>So if something happens to them, how can I continue going on? And I kept wondering how my life will be if that's actually my child.
<v Interpreter>所以如果他们发生了什么事，我怎么能继续活下去？我一直想知道如果那真的是我的孩子，我的生活会是什么样子。

00:53:37.000 --> 00:53:47.190
<v Kimu Elolia>Finally, at around 9:00 PM, one of Ospina's friends called. Ospina was OK. Anna rushed out to meet him, and she found him in the middle of the street.
<v Kimu Elolia>终于，在晚上9点左右，奥斯皮纳的一个朋友打了电话。奥斯皮纳没事。安娜冲出去见他，她在街中间找到了他。

00:53:47.190 --> 00:53:48.560
<v Anna>[SPEAKING SWAHILI]
<v Anna>（斯瓦希里语发言）

00:53:48.560 --> 00:54:12.470
<v Interpreter>The first thing I told him, like, I thank god that you are still alive, but please don't ever go back to the protests. And he said, I have to go. And I told him, listen to me, I'm your parent. If something happens to you, Kenya is not losing anything. I am the person that's losing. I'm losing you.
<v Interpreter>我告诉他的第一件事，比如，我感谢上帝你还活着，但请永远不要再回抗议现场了。他说，我必须去。我对他说，听着，我是你的父母。如果如果你发生什么事，肯尼亚不会失去任何东西。失去的人是我。我失去的是你。

00:54:12.470 --> 00:54:35.290
<v Interpreter>But he was adamant that he has to go back. He was, like, high with energy, explaining everything that happened with so much gusto. And meanwhile, I'm shaking. And I'm like, this child doesn't know what he put me through.
<v Interpreter>但他坚持他必须回去。他就像是被能量打过兴奋剂一样，解释着发生的一切，热情洋溢。与此同时，我在发抖。我想，这个孩子不知道他让我经历了什么。

00:54:35.290 --> 00:54:53.650
<v Ospina>Yeah, I mean, it just made me feel like she just doesn't understand why I'm doing whatever I'm doing. I mean, my mom is not comfortable with me being an activist because she's like, just relax. Have a family, you know? So, I mean, that is why sometimes we don't get along. And I find it so difficult sometimes to keep on repeating it.
<v Ospina>是的，我的意思是，这让我觉得她就是不明白我为什么要那样做。我的意思是，我妈妈不舒服我成为一名活动家，因为她心想，放松点。成个家，你知道吗？所以，这就是为什么有时候我们相处不来。我发现有时候一遍又一遍重复它太困难了。

00:54:53.650 --> 00:55:18.850
<v Kimu Elolia>Ospina felt like, I'm responsible, and I do everything I can to get home safely. He wished his mom could see that. He went back to his place and turned off his phone, shutting everyone out.
<v Kimu Elolia>奥斯皮纳觉得，我是有责任的，我尽我所能安全回家。他希望他妈妈能看到这一点。他回到住处关掉了电话，把每个人都隔绝在外。

00:55:18.850 --> 00:55:32.480
<v Kimu Elolia>Two days later, Ospina stopped by Anna's chapati stand with some of his friends and told her they were headed to another demonstration. In front of everyone on the street, including his friends, Anna dropped to her knees.
<v Kimu Elolia>两天后，奥斯皮纳带着一些朋友顺路来到安娜的查帕蒂摊位，告诉她他们正要去参加另一次示威。在街上的每个人面前，包括他的朋友们，安娜跪了下来。

00:55:32.480 --> 00:55:35.770
<v Anna>[SPEAKING SWAHILI]
<v Anna>（斯瓦希里语发言）

00:55:35.770 --> 00:55:45.810
<v Interpreter>I knew that I had to do something that will make them think, what has made Mom go down on her knees? Maybe this is something we should rethink.
<v Interpreter>我知道我必须做些什么让他们思考，是什么让妈妈跪下来了？也许这是我们应该重新考虑的事情。

00:55:45.810 --> 00:55:52.640
<v Kimu Elolia>Mm. That's such a vulnerable thing to do. Some people would feel humiliated.
<v Kimu Elolia>嗯。那真是非常脆弱的表现。有些人会觉得屈辱。

00:55:52.640 --> 00:55:56.620
<v Anna>[SPEAKING SWAHILI]
<v Anna>（斯瓦希里语发言）

00:55:56.620 --> 00:56:00.740
<v Interpreter>I didn't care about shame. In fact, people were laughing. Spectators were laughing.
<v Interpreter>我不在乎羞耻。事实上，人们在笑。围观者在笑。

00:56:00.740 --> 00:56:01.400
<v Kimu Elolia>Really?
<v Kimu Elolia>真的吗？

00:56:01.400 --> 00:56:02.040
<v Interpreter>Yeah.
<v Interpreter>是的。

00:56:02.040 --> 00:56:03.440
<v Kimu Elolia>They were laughing?
<v Kimu Elolia>他们在笑？

00:56:03.440 --> 00:56:12.380
<v Interpreter>They were laughing, pointing at me, telling each other, look, Mama Chapati is so afraid. His kids are going to go and protest.
<v Interpreter>他们在笑，指着我，互相说，看，妈妈查帕蒂太害怕了。他的孩子要去抗议。

00:56:12.380 --> 00:56:15.540
<v Kimu Elolia>What did you see in his face at that moment?
<v Kimu Elolia>那一刻你在他的脸上看到了什么？

00:56:15.540 --> 00:56:18.950
<v Anna>[SPEAKING SWAHILI]
<v Anna>（斯瓦希里语发言）

00:56:18.950 --> 00:56:25.890
<v Interpreter>So in his face, I saw denial. It's like he did not want to hear me say what I wanted to say.
<v Interpreter>所以在他脸上，我看到了否认。好像他不想听到我想说的话。

00:56:25.890 --> 00:56:27.740
<v Kimu Elolia>Mm, so--
<v Kimu Elolia>嗯，所以——

00:56:27.740 --> 00:56:28.950
<v Interpreter>Yeah.
<v Interpreter>是的。

00:56:28.950 --> 00:56:32.010
<v Anna>[SPEAKING SWAHILI]
<v Anna>（斯瓦希里语发言）

00:56:32.010 --> 00:56:34.280
<v Ospina>I mean, it was so insane. I just had to leave.
<v Ospina>我的意思是，那太疯狂了。我不得不离开。

00:56:34.280 --> 00:56:36.440
<v Kimu Elolia>Oh, you walked out?
<v Kimu Elolia>哦，你走开了？

00:56:36.440 --> 00:56:38.120
<v Ospina>Yeah, I just walked out.
<v Ospina>是的，我就走开了。

00:56:38.120 --> 00:56:39.260
<v Kimu Elolia>Why?
<v Kimu Elolia>为什么？

00:56:39.260 --> 00:56:57.420
<v Ospina>I've never seen such a thing. And from my understanding, it's not allowed to be happening. So I was like, this is so weird. So I cannot just stay there because I don't know the best thing to do. I can't comfort her. I can't explain anything, you know.
<v Ospina>我从未见过这样的事。据我理解，这种事是不允许发生的。所以我心想，这太奇怪了。所以我不能就待在那儿，因为我不知道最好的办法是什么。我不能安慰她。我不能解释任何事，你知道。

00:56:57.420 --> 00:57:08.280
<v Kimu Elolia>Ospina walked away, went to the protests. But that night, the image of his mom kneeling, begging, it weighed on his mind.
<v Kimu Elolia>奥斯皮纳走开了，去了抗议现场。但那天晚上，他妈妈下跪乞求的画面在他脑海中挥之不去。

00:57:08.280 --> 00:57:25.060
<v Ospina>That was massive because, I mean, I felt like she'd gone too low. I actually found it so difficult to sleep. I had a lot of anxiety. Then I was like, I need to take some few break, reflect, and make a good choice.
<v Ospina>那太震撼了，因为我的意思是，我觉得她已经卑微到了极点。我实际上发现很难入睡。我非常焦虑。我心想，我需要休息一下，反思一下，做出一个好的选择。

00:57:25.060 --> 00:57:28.540
<v Kimu Elolia>The next day, Ospina went to visit his mom.
<v Kimu Elolia>第二天，奥斯皮纳去探望他的母亲。

00:57:28.540 --> 00:57:39.950
<v Ospina>First of all, I started by apologizing for not listening, putting her in that situation and all the emotion to make me feel like I'm listening to her.
<v Ospina>首先，我从道歉开始，为没有听她的话，让她陷入那种境地，所有那些情感道歉，让我感觉到我在倾听她。

00:57:39.950 --> 00:57:42.420
<v Kimu Elolia>Did you promise her anything in that moment?
<v Kimu Elolia>那一刻你向她承诺了什么吗？

00:57:42.420 --> 00:58:02.150
<v Ospina>Yes. First, I promised to just to tell her the truth, that anytime I'll be going for the protest, I'll be letting her know. Then anytime I felt like it was so dangerous, I will not be going. If it's bad, I will just be there for a few moments, and I'll try to be very responsible.
<v Ospina>是的。首先，我承诺只是告诉她真相，每当我去抗议时，我会告诉她。然后每当我感到它太危险时，我就不会去。如果情况很糟，我只会待一会儿，我会尽量表现得非常负责。

00:58:02.150 --> 00:58:06.650
<v Kimu Elolia>Did she feel like that was good enough for her?
<v Kimu Elolia>她觉得这对他来说足够了吗？

00:58:06.650 --> 00:58:08.270
<v Ospina>No, not really.
<v Ospina>不，没有。

00:58:08.270 --> 00:58:11.900
<v Kimu Elolia>Do you know what else-- what else did she want to hear?
<v Kimu Elolia>你知道还有什么——她还想听到什么？

00:58:11.900 --> 00:58:17.250
<v Ospina>She just wanted to hear [LAUGHS] I will not go. I will never go again.
<v Ospina>她只是想听到（笑）我不会去的。我再也不会去了。

00:58:17.250 --> 00:58:23.660
<v Kimu Elolia>Even though Anna didn't get what she wanted-- Ospina would continue to go to the protests-- she was satisfied.
<v Kimu Elolia>尽管安娜没有得到她想要的——奥斯皮纳将继续去抗议——但她满足了。

00:58:23.660 --> 00:58:25.200
<v Anna>[SPEAKING SWAHILI]
<v Anna>（斯瓦希里语发言）

00:58:25.200 --> 00:58:31.020
<v Interpreter>Yeah, so I saw that, now, he's listening. And yeah.
<v Interpreter>是的，所以我看到，现在，他在听了。是的。

00:58:31.020 --> 00:58:33.630
<v Anna>[SPEAKING SWAHILI]
<v Anna>（斯瓦希里语发言）

00:58:33.630 --> 00:58:36.640
<v Interpreter>I was so happy. I had to be happy.
<v Interpreter>我太开心了。我必须开心。

00:58:36.640 --> 00:58:39.000
<v Kimu Elolia>Yeah. Did you celebrate?
<v Kimu Elolia>是的。你们庆祝了吗？

00:58:39.000 --> 00:58:40.260
<v Anna>[SPEAKING SWAHILI]
<v Anna>（斯瓦希里语发言）

00:58:40.260 --> 00:58:42.930
<v Interpreter>A lot.
<v Interpreter>很多。

00:58:42.930 --> 00:58:56.420
<v Kimu Elolia>That night, she cooked a special meal for Ospina and her entire family.
<v Kimu Elolia>那天晚上，她为奥斯皮纳和她的整个家庭做了一顿特别的饭。

00:58:56.420 --> 00:59:08.490
<v Kimu Elolia>In the weeks after the parliament protests, the president actually made some pretty big concessions, but not enough for the protesters, who still want him out. They're still on the streets, and it's gotten more intense.
<v Kimu Elolia>在议会抗议后的几周里，总统实际上做出了一些相当大的让步，但对那些仍想让他下台的抗议者来说还不够。他们还在街上，情况变得更加紧张。

00:59:08.490 --> 00:59:27.290
<v Kimu Elolia>Amnesty International says that at least 49 people have been abducted by the government. Protesters have been disappeared, with a couple showing up dead. At first, the government denied any involvement, but now, President Ruto is at least talking about possible investigations.
<v Kimu Elolia>国际特赦组织表示，至少有49人被政府绑架。抗议者失踪了，有几个人被发现死了。起初，政府否认有任何参与，但现在，鲁托总统至少在谈论可能的调查。

00:59:27.290 --> 00:59:39.050
<v Kimu Elolia>Ospina skipped a couple of protests because they seemed too dangerous, like a planned march to the Nairobi airport. But he is having a hard time keeping all of his promises to Anna.
<v Kimu Elolia>奥斯皮纳错过了几次抗议，因为它们看起来太危险了，比如计划好的向内罗毕机场的游行。但他很难遵守对安娜的所有承诺。

00:59:39.050 --> 00:59:41.390
<v Anna>[SPEAKING SWAHILI]
<v Anna>（斯瓦希里语发言）

00:59:41.390 --> 00:59:59.390
<v Interpreter>So there are times when he disappears for a whole day. And then when he comes back, I'm like, I know you went to the protest. And sometimes, he'll admit and be like, OK, fine. I went, but I wasn't in the front lines. I was at the very back.
<v Interpreter>所以有时候他会整天失踪。然后当他回来时，我心想，我知道你去抗议了。有时候，他会承认，就像，好的，好吧。我去过，但我没在前线。我在最后面。

00:59:59.390 --> 01:00:01.610
<v Kimu Elolia>Do you believe that he was at the back?
<v Kimu Elolia>你相信他在后面吗？

01:00:01.610 --> 01:00:03.770
<v Anna>[SPEAKING SWAHILI]
<v Anna>（斯瓦希里语发言）

01:00:03.770 --> 01:00:07.580
<v Interpreter>I don't believe it at all, not for a second.
<v Interpreter>我一点也不相信，一秒钟也不信。

01:00:07.580 --> 01:00:13.700
<v Kimu Elolia>How does it make you feel that he lies to you about going to the protest?
<v Kimu Elolia>他向你隐瞒去抗议这件事，这让你感觉如何？

01:00:13.700 --> 01:00:18.140
<v Anna>[SPEAKING SWAHILI]
<v Anna>（斯瓦希里语发言）

01:00:18.140 --> 01:00:24.660
<v Interpreter>I'm so annoyed by that, by the lies. And I'm so afraid for him.
<v Interpreter>我对谎言感到非常恼火。而且我为他感到非常害怕。

01:00:24.660 --> 01:00:32.100
<v Kimu Elolia>Mm. He told us that he lies to you because he doesn't want to burden you. How does that make you feel?
<v Kimu Elolia>嗯。他告诉我们他向你撒谎是因为他不想给你带来负担。这让你感觉如何？

01:00:32.100 --> 01:00:33.420
<v Anna>[SPEAKING SWAHILI]
<v Anna>（斯瓦希里语发言）

01:00:33.420 --> 01:00:44.670
<v Interpreter>I just keep wondering why he wants to die so early, and he has so much to do. Why?
<v Interpreter>我只是不停地想，为什么他想死得这么早，他还有那么多事情要做。为什么？

01:00:44.670 --> 01:01:04.100
<v Kimu Elolia>So here they both are. He's not going to change, and she's not going to feel better about it. So he keeps heading off into danger, and she keeps hoping for the best. And the protests just continue.
<v Kimu Elolia>所以他们都在这里。他不会改变，她也不会感觉更好。所以他继续冲向危险，而她继续祈祷一切顺利。抗议活动还在继续。

01:01:04.100 --> 01:01:15.450
<v Ira Glass>Kimu Elolia. This story was produced by Emmanuel Dzotsi with additional reporting by Henry Larson. Vincho Nchogu translated what Anna was saying. Additional translation by Happiness Bulugu.
<v Ira Glass>金木·埃洛利亚。这个故事由伊曼纽尔·佐齐制作，亨利·拉尔森进行补充报道。文乔·恩乔古翻译了安娜的话。额外的翻译由哈皮内斯·布鲁古提供。

01:01:15.450 --> 01:02:03.360
<v Ira Glass>["THE SHARK FIGHTER!" BY THE AQUABATS!]
<v Ira Glass>（《鲨鱼斗士！》-水族人乐队）

